    "created_at": "2018-08-24T08:33:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-24T08:33:18Z",
    "body": "Not extending the safelist for UA generated values would add a significant cost to introducing any new request headers. That makes little sense. (For both CH as well as other UA generated headers. e.g. `upgrade-insecure-requests`).\r\n\r\nPreflights don't come for free, and we should carefully consider the (infinitesimal IMO) risk of sending newly-introduced UA generated headers (with value restrictions) to servers vs. the certainty of inflicting performance pain on all/many users as a result.\r\n\r\n/cc @mikewest\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
